    {
      "id": 243458,
      "name": "TyphonLLC",
      "username": "TyphonLLC",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/typhonllc/{size}/2087_2.png",
      "created_at": "2022-03-13T14:48:51.593Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Hi.</p>\n<p>Maybe this should be a new post, but my questions start from a Cheapass Games perspective.</p>\n<p>I was a Demo Monkey for Cheapass Games. And took their games to multiple board games stores (around Columbus Ohio) at least once a month.</p>\n<p>I guess when GTG bought Cheapass, I was transferred over to their Citizens Program? Maybe?</p>\n<p>I spoke to someone at Origins 2019, and was told to check ‘something’ out and details would follow on how I could Demo for GTG.</p>\n<p>Then Pandemic.</p>\n<p>Needless to say I’m not sure where/how to access the Citizens Program? But I bought Definitive Edition of Sentials and was hoping to be able to demo the game.I also would love to keep demoing all my Cheapass Games.</p>\n<p>Where do I go to get certified to Demo? Is there a place to record Demos? Is there a reward program for doing demos? Help?</p>\n<p>(I’ve gone to the Facebook Citizens page, but that just seems like one person posting links to marvel games???)</p>\n<p>Any direction is appreciated. And will there be a booth/volunteers needed for Origins this year?</p>\n<p>Thanks.</p>",
      "post_number": 8,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2022-03-13T14:48:51.593Z",
      "reply_count": 2,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 1,
      "reads": 31,
      "readers_count": 30,
      "score": 21.2,
      "yours": false,
      "topic_id": 29144,
      "topic_slug": "whats-going-on-with-cheapass-games",
      "display_username": "TyphonLLC",
      "primary_group_name": null,
      "flair_name": null,
      "flair_url": null,
      "flair_bg_color": null,
      "flair_color": null,
      "flair_group_id": null,
      "badges_granted": [],
      "version": 1,
      "can_edit": false,
